    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19266" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gallŏgraeci</span></b> ,
		ōrum, m.
		Galli-Graeci, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the Gauls who migrated into Phrygia</i>, called
			also Galatae, <i><span class="en">Mel. 1, 2, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 37,
			40</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Flor. 2, 11,
			3</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Deriv. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gallŏgraecĭa</span></b> , ae,
				f., <i>the country of the</i>
			Gallograeci, <i>called also</i> Galatia (v. Galatae,
			II. A.), <i><span class="en">Caes. B. C. 3, 4, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 38,
			12</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Flor. 2, 11, 1</span></i>.</div>
